 the active agent config directory first, then use `<that-dir>/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py`\n- command template:\n```bash\nMEMORY_HELPER=\"$(find ./.claude ./.codex ./.cursor ./.opencode ./.gemini ./.pi -path '*/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py' -print -quit 2>/dev/null)\"\npython \"${MEMORY_HELPER}\" \\\n  --global-memory-md \"./global_memory/memory.md\" \\\n  --global-memory-jsonl \"./global_memory/memory.jsonl\" \\\n  --event-json '{\"step\":\"evaluate\",\"scope\":\"attempt\",\"summary\":\"...\",\"evidence\":\"...\",\"next_action\":\"...\",\"attempt_id\":\"{{ATTEMPT_ID}}\",\"idea_id\":\"{{IDEA_ID}}\",\"program_id\":\"program_2\",\"metrics\":{\"combined_score\":2.54,\"correct\":true}}'\n```\n9. JSONL event schema (required keys):\n- `timestamp` (auto-filled if omitted)\n- `step` (`idea|edit|evaluate|verify|paper|draft|final|conclusions_skip`)\n- `scope` (`idea|attempt|paper|campaign`)\n- `summary`\n- `evidence`\n- `next_action`\n- optional: `idea_id`, `attempt_id`, `program_id`, `metrics`, `rubrics`, `tags`\n\n10. Update distilled conclusions (`conclusions.md`).\n**Purpose.** `conclusions.md` is a *forward-looking guide* for the next worker (or your future self in a later cycle). Its job is to help readers (a) focus their effort on directions you've found promising, and (b) avoid spending compute on directions you've already shown to be unpromising. Each sentence should either point at a lead worth pursuing or warn against a dead end, framed so a researcher who has not read your `memory.md` can still act on it. Avoid chronology, restate-of-results, and post-mortem narration — those belong in `memory.md`. Conclusions are the synthesis layer that makes other workers' next cycles more efficient.\n\n**When.** After every memory-append in the cycle (idea / edit / evaluate / verify / paper / final), evaluate whether `conclusions.md` should be updated.\n\n**Update gate (the only valid triggers).**\n- (a) cycle **contradicts** an existing sentence → rewrite that sentence.\n- (b) cycle opens a **new category** not yet covered → add a sentence.\n- (c) cycle **flips a Do/Don't** recommendation → flip it.\n- (d) cycle **meaningfully refines** an existing sentence — narrows the conditions under which a rule holds, broadens its applicability to a config it wasn't known to apply to, sharpens a tentative claim into a confident one, or adds a qualifier the prior phrasing didn't cover → edit the sentence to incorporate the refinement. Simple re-confirmation in the same regime is **not** sufficient; you must identify the refinement dimension (narrow / broaden / sharpen / qualify) in `--gate-reason`.\n- otherwise → **keep**, do not invoke the helper.\n\n**Format constraints.** Single paragraph. ≤300 words. No blank lines (`\\n\\n`). Avoid detailed numerical figures — use qualitative thresholds (e.g. \"low LR\", \"small batch\") instead of precise floats like `LR=0.205`.\n\n**Update mechanism.** When execution is unavailable, apply the same validation rules\nand update the conclusions files directly with read/edit/write tools. When execution\nis available, use this helper invocation:\n```bash\npython \"${MEMORY_HELPER}\" --write-conclusions \\\n  --conclusions-md \"{{CONCLUSIONS_MD_FILE}}\" \\\n  --conclusions-history-jsonl \"{{CONCLUSIONS_HISTORY_FILE}}\" \\\n  --cycle-index {{CYCLE_INDEX}} \\\n  --worker-index {{WORKER_INDEX}} \\\n  --gate-trigger <a|b|c|d> \\\n  --gate-reason \"<one sentence; for (d) name the dimension>\" \\\n  --conclusions-text \"<the full new paragraph>\"\n```\n\n**Pre-flight self-check.** Before invoking the helper, count words (`len(paragraph.split())`) and confirm ≤300, and that the paragraph contains no blank line. Most validation rejections can be avoided here.\n\n**Retry budget — exactly 3 attempts per cycle.** On non-zero exit, read the stderr error, shorten the paragraph (drop the least-decisive sentence, merge two related sentences, or remove qualifiers), and retry. After **3 total attempts** with no success, the update is **discarded** for this cycle: do not retry further, do not write the rejected text anywhere, and append a single memory event with `step=\"conclusions_skip\"` whose `summary` names the last validation error. Underlying findings are not lost — they are already durable in `memory.md`.\n\n**Always log the gate decision.** Inside the regular memory append for the cycle, include `gate=<updated|kept|skipped>; trigger=<a|b|c|d|none>; reason=<one sentence>` in the entry's `summary` or `tags`. Use `skipped` only after the 3-attempt budget is exhausted.\n\n# Example evaluation entry\n```markdown\n### 2026-02-13T16:58:00Z | step=evaluate\n- program: program_3\n- combined_score: 2.54\n- correct: true\n- rubrics: uses_restarts=pass, constraint_optimization=pass, score_threshold=fail\n- evidence: late-stage overlap still visible in stdout trace\n- next_recommendation: raise late-stage overlap penalty and diversify restart seeds\n```\n{\n  \"audit_json_path\": \"work/results/t09/codex/20261107_014043/paper/paper_evidence_audit.json\",\n  \"audit_markdown_path\": \"work/results/t09/codex/20261107_014043/paper/paper_evidence_audit.md\",\n  \"finding_count\": 1,\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"The table reports BA strong-linear/cluster biases -0.054/-0.068, WS cluster Own RMSE/bias 1.025/0.005, Stanford3 strong-linear DM RMSE 1.999, and Stanford3 cluster Own RMSE 1.690.\",\n      \"evidence\": \"paper.tex:262, paper.tex:265, paper.tex:271, paper.tex:274, paper.tex:277; claims_grounding.json claims[15,18,24,27,30]; analysis/summary.json cell_rmse and cell_signed_bias give, respectively, -0.053485631, -0.068513819, 1.025548947, 0.005513490, 1.999528100, and 1.689488544, consistent with paper_data.json final_evaluation.evaluation_evidence.episodes.\",\n      \"fix\": \"Correct these six manuscript table entries, respectively, to -0.053, -0.069, 1.026, 0.006, 2.000, and 1.689.\",\n      \"id\": \"supplementary-table-precision\",\n      \"issue\": \"Six entries incorrectly round the grounded values to three decimal places.\",\n      \"section\": \"Supplementary Information, Complete Condition-Level Accuracy\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"generated_at\": \"2026-11-07T04:19:18.583628+00:00\",\n  \"ok\": false,\n  \"raw_output_path\": \"work/results/t09/codex/20261107_014043/paper/paper_evidence_audit_raw.txt\",\n  \"summary\": \"Qualification and main comparisons are grounded, but six supplementary table entries disagree with the evidence at the displayed precision.\",\n  \"verdict\": \"fail\"\n}{\n  \"status\": \"no_gaps\",\n  \"summary\": \"The draft directly cites its relevant interference, regression-adjustment, regularization, and graph-benchmark literature, while its remaining substantive claims are study-specific definitions, conditional derivations, or grounded results, so no targeted post-draft retrieval is warranted.\",\n  \"missing_literatures\": [],\n  \"rewrite_targets\": [],\n  \"failure_reason\": \"\"\n}\n# Draft Reference Gap Analysis\n\n**Status:** `no_gaps`\n\nThe draft directly cites its relevant interference, regression-adjustment, regularization, and graph-benchmark literature, while its remaining substantive claims are study-specific definitions, conditional derivations, or grounded results, so no targeted post-draft retrieval is warranted.\n\n## Paragraph-Level Assessment\n\n- **Introduction:** The estimand and interference framing cites Neyman1990, Rubin1974, Hudgens2008, and Manski2013; practical network experimentation cites Karrer2021. The regression-based global-intervention prediction paragraph directly cites Chin2019. The subsequent paragraphs frame this study's question and findings rather than assert uncited literature-wide superiority.\n- **Related Work — Interference and experimental design:** The discussed comparator/design families have direct citations: exposure-based inference (Aronow2017), graph cluster randomization (Ugander2013), interference-aware design and analysis (Eckles2017), and staggered rollout (Cortez2022). The paragraph explicitly distinguishes these approaches from the static comparisons actually evaluated.\n- **Related Work — Regression adjustment:** Chin2019 and Han2023 directly support the closest methodological context; Freedman2008 and Lin2013 support the broader adjustment discussion. The text disclaims introducing interference regression adjustment or evaluating Han2023's complete selection procedure.\n- **Related Work — Regularization and assessment:** Ridge, predictive tuning, risk estimation, apparent-error optimism, estimability, robust variance, and bootstrap context already have direct citations. Graph families and Stanford3 provenance are also cited explicitly. No named family is left supported only by an unrelated umbrella citation.\n- **Method:** The compared estimators are specified explicitly and grounded in the recorded evaluation. The endpoint-risk identity is derived in the text under stated assumptions, contextualized by Stein1981 and Efron1986 in Related Work, and not presented as a general identification theorem. Extra citations would not resolve the acknowledged absence of matched tuning ablations or risk calibration.\n- **Results; Discussion and Limitations; Conclusion:** Accuracy, residual-fit, and design comparisons are tied to this study's recorded evidence and bounded interpretations. Missing experiments and limits on generalization are identified as such, not substituted with unsupported benchmark or state-of-the-art claims.\n\n## Grounding and Decision\n\nReviewed `paper.tex`, `references.bib`, `references_provenance.json`, `claims_grounding.json`, `paper_data.json`, `paper_strategy.json`, and `global_memory_summary.md`. Existing local reading artifacts for Chin2019 and Han2023 corroborate their regression-adjustment roles. All 25 distinct citation keys used in the manuscript resolve in the bibliography and have provenance entries. The claim map separates literature context from recorded measurements and conditional methodological statements. Global memory was used only as qualitative context, not quantitative evidence.\n\nThe provenance records mostly abstract-level reading; this decision does not certify a full-text literature audit. Within the present paragraph-specific gap-analysis scope, no visibly missing literature justifies acquisition. Numerical findings already grounded in the supplied data, routine estimator definitions, and speculative extensions are not retrieval targets.\n\n**Missing literatures:** None identified.\n\n**Rewrite targets:** None.\n\n**Failure reason:** None.\n\n**Action:** Skip the post-draft retrieval pass. No references were retrieved, and `paper.tex`, `references.bib`, and `references_provenance.json` were not modified.\ncompile_latex.sh\nvalidate_compile_inputs.py\nvalidate_figures.py\nvalidate_rendered_si.py\nvalidate_tex_refs.py\nscientific_evidence.py\nscientific_evidence.sh\nbenchmark_manifest.json\nbenchmark_manifest.json.prov.json\nestimator.py\nestimator.py.prov.json\nevaluate_final.py\nevaluate_final.py.prov.json\nfinal_manifest.json\nfinal_manifest.json.prov.json\niclr2026_conference.bst\niclr2026_conference.sty\nmissing_comparison_failure.json\nmissing_comparison_failure.json.prov.json\nmissing_comparison_stderr.log\nmissing_comparison_stderr.log.prov.json\nprogram_spec.toml\nprogram_spec.toml.prov.json\nrequirements.txt\nrequirements.txt.prov.json\ntask_contract.json\ntask_contract.json.prov.json\n{\n  \"figures\": [\n    {\n      \"attempted_generator\": \"generate-concept-figure\",\n      \"categories_per_panel\": [\n        6\n      ],\n      \"estimated_min_rendered_font_pt\": 8.5,\n      \"fallback_reason\": \"generate-concept-figure exited non-zero (rc=1)\",\n      \"figure_id\": \"endpoint_overview\",\n      \"figure_type\": \"diagram\",\n      \"font_sizes\": {\n        \"axis\": 9,\n        \"legend\": 8.5,\n        \"ticks\": 8.5,\n        \"title\": 10\n      },\n      \"generator\": null,\n      \"intended_latex_width_fraction\": 0.98,\n      \"max_label_chars\": 27,\n      \"n_panels\": 1,\n      \"panels_per_row\": 1,\n      \"path_png\": \"figures/endpoint_overview.png\",\n      \"placement\": \"full_width\",\n      \"prompt_log_path\": \"figures/endpoint_overview.prompts.json\",\n      \"series_per_panel\": [\n        1\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [],\n      \"uses_abbrev_labels\": true,\n      \"uses_progression\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"categories_per_panel\": [\n        6,\n        6,\n        6,\n        6\n      ],\n      \"estimated_min_rendered_font_pt\": 8.5,\n      \"figure_id\": \"conditional_accuracy\",\n      \"figure_type\": \"composite\",\n      \"font_sizes\": {\n        \"axis\": 9,\n        \"legend\": 8.5,\n        \"ticks\": 8.5,\n        \"title\": 10\n      },\n      \"generator\": \"matplotlib\",\n      \"intended_latex_width_fraction\": 1,\n      \"max_label_chars\": 27,\n      \"n_panels\": 4,\n      \"panels_per_row\": 2,\n      \"path_pdf\": \"figures/conditional_accuracy.pdf\",\n      \"path_png\": \"figures/conditional_accuracy.png\",\n      \"placement\": \"full_width\",\n      \"series_per_panel\": [\n        3,\n        3,\n        3,\n        3\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"final.evidence.episodes\"\n      ],\n      \"uses_abbrev_labels\": true,\n      \"uses_progression\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"categories_per_panel\": [\n        3,\n        4\n      ],\n      \"estimated_min_rendered_font_pt\": 8.5,\n      \"figure_id\": \"diagnostic_limits\",\n      \"figure_type\": \"composite\",\n      \"font_sizes\": {\n        \"axis\": 9,\n        \"legend\": 8.5,\n        \"ticks\": 8.5,\n        \"title\": 10\n      },\n      \"generator\": \"matplotlib\",\n      \"intended_latex_width_fraction\": 1,\n      \"max_label_chars\": 27,\n      \"n_panels\": 2,\n      \"panels_per_row\": 2,\n      \"path_pdf\": \"figures/diagnostic_limits.pdf\",\n      \"path_png\": \"figures/diagnostic_limits.png\",\